    "https://bi.easycruit.com/vacancy/3638981/45441?iso=no": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Handelshøyskolen BI Institutt for strategi og entreprenørskap - Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship - Assistant Professor Assistant Professor Send application BI Norwegian Business School (BI) invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor at the Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship. There are 2 positions available. Early career candidates hired as Assistant Professors will go through a required tenure-track process based on set criteria for publications and teaching. BI’s foundation is to be research-based, connected, and learning-oriented in order to both offer relevant programs for our students, and provide a motivating research environment for our faculty. The Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship at BI focuses on the academic fields of strategy, international business, innovation, and entrepreneurship. The Department is academically and practically relevant through high quality research and active collaboration with business and society. Key research topics include (but are not restricted to) business models, international strategy and organization, entrepreneurship, alliances, networks, acquisitions, health innovations, knowledge-based strategy, strategy processes, clusters and institutional frameworks, technological innovation, and digitalization. Teaching is based on cutting edge research, demonstrating practical relevance, and developing students’ academic competence and skills. The Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship has 58 faculty represented at all Campuses. 45% of the faculty are international, and the percentage of female faculty members is 45%. Job description The Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship wishes to expand its research-focused faculty at Campus Oslo. We are looking for candidates with strong research capabilities in topics related to our department. The ideal candidates should have ambitions to advance the field with publications in top international journals and demonstrate solid teaching skills. Applicants must document strong pipelines of high-quality research. It is expected that the person appointed has the ability and willingness to actively contribute to the department's academic community. Our faculty is expected to provide teaching and supervision of a high academic and pedagogical quality as well as continuously develop their teaching skills, e.g. by making use of new technology, new ways of learning, case-based teaching, and new forms of assessment. The desirable candidates can take on teaching assignments across a wide range of study programs. It is desirable that candidates can contribute to research and courses related to digital business, platform firms, artificial intelligence (AI), and business analytics. We also deliver a wide range of executive courses. Executive teaching experience is weighted positively. Expectations and obligations Our faculty is expected to provide teaching and supervision of a high academic and pedagogical quality and is expected to continuously develop their teaching skills, e.g. by making use of new technology, new ways of learning and new forms of assessment. We have focus on quality and competence development and pedagogical activities should be continuously documented, supporting the process for further academic career development to all positions. For all positions with research duties BI have high expectations for research production. Failing to meet the expectations could lead to increased duties in teaching. Those employed in a scientific position will also have teaching and pedagogical development responsibilities. In addition to traditional teaching, the position includes development of courses, learning activities, forms of evaluation, and guidance. Qualification Requirements Scientific positions A PhD in an academically relevant discipline (preference is given to candidates focusing their research on digital business strategies, platform firms, and AI as well as documented teaching experience related to business analytics and AI). A demonstrated ability to publish in high-quality international academic journals. Documented teaching experience or pedagogical development. Other assessment criteria Language skills; English written and oral (Norwegian if relevant). All pedagogical and research positions must document language proficiency, according to Norwegian law, in Norwegian at minimum the B2 level or be subject to acquiring the level within 3 years of the appointment. Good communication skills Visibility within the international and national academic community is desirable, for instance: Papers must regularly appear in top international conferences, and well-recognized journals/outlets within the relevant discipline/area. Be visible on the academic arena or other relevant arenas important for the discipline. Industry experience is valued. The following qualifications will be also considered in the assessment of the applicants: Documented experience with interactive and process-oriented teaching methods. Knowledge of and interest in modern pedagogical approaches, as well as the development of study programs, will be appreciated. Weight will also be given to experience from public sector, business and/or the public sector, including R&D work, research dissemination and research-based advisory services. International work experience in the field of strategy, innovation, entrepreneurship, and international business is valued. According to governmental provisions BI has decided on requirements concerning the educational qualifications of permanently employed academic staff. As a minimum such qualifications shall meet the learning outcome of BI‘s pedagogical basic qualification courses or equivalent at all times. The required specific competence must be attained within two years of appointment as Associate Professor. What we can offer The position normally offers membership in BIs collective pension scheme. A good working environment at one of Scandinavia's leading business schools. Good research support and publication remuneration. A supportive and research-active community at one of Scandinavia's leading business schools. Pedagogical support and opportunities to teach across levels and programs. Relocation services for you and your family (if applicable ). Application procedure Qualifications will be evaluated according to the usual rules for academic positions at universities and specialized university institutions, as well as BI provisions for appointment and promotion. Candidates interested in this position must submit their application electronically through the “ Send application ” button, and upload the following documents: Cover letter CV and publication list Certificate from the highest degree obtained Scientific statement with future research plans Scientific works and pedagogical dissemination articles (up to 15 works) Statement of teaching philosophy with supporting documentation showing pedagogical qualifications Other documentation that may be important for assessing the level of competence Two letters of reference Work may not be submitted after the deadline. Women are encouraged to apply. BI Norwegian Business School is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants may be called in for an interview, trial lecture or seminar presentation. BI Norwegian Business School reserves the right not to appoint applicants who are academically qualified if they are found not to satisfy other explicit requirements with respect to pedagogical skills, teaching experience, work experience in or in cooperation with the business sector or inter-personal skills. Further information For further information regarding the recruitment process, documentation requirements, and evaluation criteria, please see this guide. Further information about the position can be obtained by contacting Birgitte Grøgaard, Head of Department, telephone +47 46410535, birgitte.grogaard@bi.no, or (if there is any other relevant contact). For more information about the department and the school visit Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship About Oslo Oslo, the capital of Norway, is an international, fast growing, and attractive city. For more information on Oslo, please visit this site Print Send application Share on: Region: Oslo Job type: Fixed Term Contract Working hours: Full-time Working days: Day Application deadline: 30/09/2026 Expected start date: Etter avtale Location: Campus Oslo Contacts: Birgitte Grøgaard Mobile: +47 46410535 Company homepage: http://www.bi.no Handelshøyskolen BI Institutt for strategi og entreprenørskap - Department of Strategy and Entrepreneurship BI Norwegian Business School is ranked as Norway’s #1 business school and one of the best in Europe. With more than 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000 alumni, it is also one of the largest and most influential business schools in Europe. BI is considered the main provider of business education in Norway, offering a diverse and comprehensive portfolio of bachelor’s, master’s, PhD and executive study programmes and courses. Our different partnerships and collaborations with leading Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions further enhance the quality of our study programmes. Towards 2030, BI aims to deliver knowledge that truly makes a difference through world-class research and outstanding learning experiences, giving businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the opportunity to build meaningful careers. Back to the top"
    },
    "https://bi.easycruit.com/vacancy/3654731/45444?iso=no": {
      "title": "Business Designer",
      "description": "Handelshøyskolen BI Digital - Business Designer Handelshøyskolen BI søker Business Designer! Business Designer Søk her Brennende opptatt av sammenhengen mellom forretning, teknologi og brukerbehov? Vi er på jakt etter en svært erfaren strategisk rådgiver med sterk teknologiforståelse som er den naturlige brobyggeren mellom forretningsbehov, teknologi, design og prosessforståelse. Rollen har ulike navn i ulike organisasjoner, men om det står Business Designer, Forretningsutvikler, Prosessanalytiker, Virksomhetsarkitekt eller Tjenestedesigner på CVen din er ikke viktig. Du kan med andre ord ha ulike faglige bakgrunner, men det viktigste er at du evner å se helheten og omsette svært komplekse problemstillinger til konkrete løsninger og prosessforbedringer. Du jobber med forretningsutvikling, forstår teknologi og har gjerne et designtankesett i bunn. Du liker å jobbe både strategisk og operativt. Den ene dagen presenterer du løsningsalternativer til nøkkelinteressenter, den neste fasiliteter du en prosessworkshop med detaljerte gjennomganger av dataflyter gjennom komplekse verdikjeder eller tester hypoteser om nye tjenester med brukere. Du er personen som forstår systemlandskapet på tvers av Digital og resten av organisasjonen — og som hjelper BI å bli mer moden i systemisk designtenkning. Sammen med produktområdelederne synliggjør du hvordan digitale løsninger er en kritisk del av prosessen, og posisjonerer BI Digital som en relevant medspiller for resten av organisasjonen. Sentrale arbeidsoppgaver Prosessdesign og verdikjedeanalyse: Kartlegge, analysere og designe helhetlige tjenester, arbeidsprosesser og verdikjeder på tvers av fagområder, avdelinger og produktteam Dataforståelse og dataflyt: Kartlegge datastrømmer og beskrive for hvordan data skal flyte gjennom integrerte løsninger Strukturere og prioritere behov og problemstillinger på tvers av fagområder og produktteam sammen med produktområdeleder Helhetlig forståelse: Se sammenhengen mellom prosesser, plattformer og organisasjonsstruktur, og identifisere systemiske utfordringer og nye løsninger Forankring, fasilitering og brobygging: Redusere silotenkning ved å fasilitere workshops, bygge tillit blant interessenter og kommunisere prosess- og arkitektur på et språk hele organisasjonen forstår. Forretningsdesign: Vurdere det forretningsmessige potensialet i nye løsninger — hvilke forretningsmodeller som kan ligge til grunn, hvilke kostnader og gevinster som er relevante, og om en løsning bør bygges Bakgrunn og erfaring Erfaring fra business design, tjenestedesign, forretningsutvikling, virksomhetsarkitektur, prosessanalyse eller tilgrensende roller i komplekse organisasjoner. Du kan gjerne ha erfaring fra flere av disse domenene. Relevant høyere utdanning, gjerne på masternivå — solid erfaring kan kompensere for formell utdanning Dokumentert evne til å kartlegge og forstå komplekse organisasjoner, verdikjeder og systemlandskap Erfaring med å jobbe med interessenter med varierende modenhet. God forståelse for digital produktutvikling og tverrfaglig samarbeid Erfaring fra komplekse kunnskapsorganisasjoner er en fordel Kjennskap til forretningsmodellering, lean canvas eller tilsvarende verktøy er en fordel Kjennskap til moderne produktmetodikk (Dual Track, Continuous Discovery, lean UX) er en fordel Personlige egenskaper Tenker strategisk og langsiktig — ser helheten i fag-, teknologi- og organisasjonsutvikling Kommuniserer tydelig og tillitskapende på tvers av svært ulike fagmiljøer og nivåer i organisasjonen Leder gjennom tillit, påvirkning og relasjoner — ikke bare formell autoritet Nysgjerrig på andres fagdisipliner og evner å se verden fra deres perspektiv Beslutningsdyktig og løsningsorientert i møte med kompleksitet og ambiguitet Verdsetter psykologisk trygghet og bygger rom der folk tør å prøve, feile og lære Hos BI tilbyr vi: Muligheten til å være med på en spennende transformasjonsreise i en av Europas ledende handelshøyskoler. En spennende stilling i et ambisiøst og faglig sterkt miljø, hvor du får mulighet til å sette retning og skape konkrete resultater. Produktorganisering der teamene har stor frihet til å finne de beste løsningene, og du vil være premissgivende for at vi lykkes i dette arbeidet. Gode muligheter til personlig utvikling, inkludert mulighet til å studere ved BI. Strukturert kompetanseutvikling, involvering i relevante faggrupper, og vi tilbyr mulighet for å ta kurs og delta på konferanser. Fantastiske kollegaer og et trivelig sosialt miljø. Konkurransedyktig lønn etter kvalifikasjoner og gode pensjons- og forsikringsordninger. Fleksibel arbeidstid og gode velferdsordninger, inkludert fri i romjula og påskeuka, i tillegg til fem ukers ferie. Arbeidssted vil være BIs campus i Oslo (Nydalen). Har du lyst til å bli kjent med oss? Send en kort søknad - vi ser frem til å høre fra deg! Har du spørsmål, ta gjerne kontakt med direktør Cathrin Hellan Solhaug, mobil 976 70 776. Skriv ut Søk her Del på: Fylke: Oslo Jobbtype: Fast Heltid/Deltid: Heltid Arbeidstid: Dag Søknadsfrist: 13.09.2026 Tiltredelse: Etter avtale Arbeidssted: Oslo Kontaktpersoner: Cathrin Helland Solhaug mob: +47 97670776 Hjemmeside: http://www.bi.no Handelshøyskolen BI Digital Handelshøyskolen BI er en internasjonal handelshøyskole i verdensklasse. Med over 20.000 studenter, 1000 ansatte og 300.000 alumni, er BI også regnet som en av de største og mest innflytelsesrike handelshøyskolene i Europa. BI tilbyr en variert og omfattende portefølje av bachelor-, master-, PhD-, og videreutdanningsprogrammer og kurs. Våre ulike partnerskap og samarbeid med ledende norske og internasjonale selskaper, organisasjoner og institusjoner bidrar til å heve kvaliteten på vårt utdanningstilbud. BIs Strategi 2030 har definert tydelige mål for å sikre at skolen leverer kunnskap som forandrer gjennom førsteklasses forskning og enestående læringsopplevelser. Vi gir virksomheter kunnskapen de trenger for å lykkes og mennesker muligheten til å bygge meningsfylte karrierer. Tilbake til toppen"
    },
    "https://bi.easycruit.com/vacancy/3661201/143965?iso=no": {
      "title": "Handelshøyskolen BI Organisasjon & Virksomhetsstyring",
      "description": "Handelshøyskolen BI Organisasjon & Virksomhetsstyring - Jurist/Seniorrådgiver Handelshøyskolen BI søker jurist/seniorrådgiver Jurist/Seniorrådgiver Søk her Jurist – vil du jobbe i skjæringspunktet mellom utdanning, forvaltning og aktuell juss? Vi søker en selvstendig og strukturert jurist til en fast stilling som seniorrådgiver. Dette er en kombinasjonsstilling som gir deg det beste fra to verdener: Du vil ha en nøkkelrolle i arbeidet med å sikre forsvarlig og effektiv behandling av klage- og fuskesaker, samtidig som du får arbeide med et bredt spekter av juridiske problemstillinger. Hos BI får du en sentral juridisk rolle med stor faglig bredde, hvor du både har ansvar for sekretariatet til BIs Nemnd for Studentsaker og bidrar inn i et kompetent juridisk team. Rollen passer for deg som trives med både grundig saksbehandling og juridisk rådgivning. Du motiveres av å ta ansvar, arbeide selvstendig og bidra i et fagmiljø der juridiske vurderinger har stor betydning for organisasjonen. Stillingen er plassert i Avdeling for virksomhetsstyring, som er en del av Enhet for organisasjon og virksomhetsstyring. Sentrale arbeidsoppgaver Som sekretær for BIs Nemnd for Studentsaker: Løpende og systematisk forberedelse og juridisk kvalitetssikring av klagesaker og fuskesaker til BIs Nemnd for Studentsaker i tråd med universitets- og høyskoleloven og forvaltningsloven. Skrive innstillinger til nemnda og nemndas vedtak etter faste maler og rutiner, og påse at innstillinger og vedtak er i samsvar med BIs gjeldende regelverk. Fungere som faglige og administrative støttespiller før, under og etter nemndas møter, og som kontaktpunkt mellom nemnda og BI. Håndtere løpende korrespondanse med studenter, advokater og interne instanser. Som medlem av Juridisk team: Håndtering og koordinering av innsynskrav etter offentleglova. Rådgivning og saksbehandling knyttet til personvern (GDPR) og informasjonssikkerhet. Bidra aktivt inn i teamets øvrige oppgaver. Du vil få mulighet til å bistå organisasjonen med variert juridisk rådgivning også utenfor kjerneområdet ditt, avhengig av hvor behovet ligger. Hvem er du? Vi ser etter en faglig trygg jurist som evner å drive prosesser fremover på egenhånd, men som også trigges av å lykkes sammen med teamet. Du har Master i rettsvitenskap eller Cand.jur. Relevant arbeidserfaring med saksbehandling og forvaltningsrett. God skriftlig og muntlig fremstillingsevne på norsk og engelsk. Det er en fordel om du har: Erfaring fra universitets- og høyskolesektoren. God kjennskap til og erfaring med forvaltningsloven God kjennskap til og erfaring med personvernregelverket (GDPR) og praktisering av offentleglova. Personlige egenskaper: Selvstendig og strukturert: Du tar eierskap til oppgavene dine, har høy faglig integritet og leverer med høy kvalitet. Sterk rolleforståelse og høy integritet: Du evner å navigere klokt og profesjonelt i rollen som bindeledd mellom BIs linjeorganisasjon og en selvstendig, uavhengig nemnd. Fleksibel og nysgjerrig: Du har en bred juridisk interesse og tar gjerne i et tak på andre rettsområder når teamet trenger det. Relasjonsbygger og formidler: Du samarbeider godt på tvers av organisasjonen. Vi tilbyr: Et godt faglig og sosialt arbeidsmiljø, med hyggelige, engasjerte og kompetente kollegaer En meget spennende organisasjon med stor aktivitet og høye ambisjoner Fleksibilitet, varierte oppgaver og mulighet til å være med å forme din egen arbeidshverdag 35 timers arbeidsuke, 5 ukers ferie, samt fri jul og påske Gode ordninger for pensjon og forsikring Arbeidssted vil være BIs campus i Oslo (Nydalen). Hvis du tror denne stillingen passer for deg, er du velkommen til å søke. Har du spørsmål, ta gjerne kontakt med seniorrådgiver Anita Tøien på mobil 41423486. Skriv ut Søk her Del på: Fylke: Oslo Jobbtype: Fast Heltid/Deltid: Heltid Arbeidstid: Dag Søknadsfrist: 27.09.2026 Tiltredelse: Etter avtale Arbeidssted: Oslo Kontaktpersoner: Anita Tøien mob: +47 41423486 Hjemmeside: https://www.bi.no/ Handelshøyskolen BI Organisasjon & Virksomhetsstyring Handelshøyskolen BI er en internasjonal handelshøyskole i verdensklasse. Med over 20.000 studenter, 1000 ansatte og 300.000 alumni, er BI også regnet som en av de største og mest innflytelsesrike handelshøyskolene i Europa. BI tilbyr en variert og omfattende portefølje av bachelor-, master-, PhD-, og videreutdanningsprogrammer og kurs. Våre ulike partnerskap og samarbeid med ledende norske og internasjonale selskaper, organisasjoner og institusjoner bidrar til å heve kvaliteten på vårt utdanningstilbud. BIs Strategi 2030 har definert tydelige mål for å sikre at skolen leverer kunnskap som forandrer gjennom førsteklasses forskning og enestående læringsopplevelser. Vi gir virksomheter kunnskapen de trenger for å lykkes og mennesker muligheten til å bygge meningsfylte karrierer. Tilbake til toppen English Latvian Danish Czech Dutch Estonian German Spanish Swedish Finnish French Italian Lithuanian Norwegian Polish × Dette nettstedet bruker informasjonskapsler Vi bruker informasjonskapsler for å tilpasse innhold, annonser og analysere trafikken vår. Vi deler også informasjon om din bruk av nettstedet vårt med våre annonserings- og analysepartnere som kan kombinere den med annen informasjon du har gitt dem eller som de har samlet inn fra din bruk av tjenestene deres. Privacy Policy Vis detaljer Skjul detaljer Lagre og lukk Godta alle Avvis alle"
    },
    "https://bi.easycruit.com/vacancy/3661897/200453?iso=no": {
      "title": "Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet",
      "description": "Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet - Doktorgrad  - PhD Candidate in Communications PhD Candidate in Communications Send application The Department of Communication and Culture at BI Norwegian Business School is currently inviting applications for multiple four-year doctoral scholarships, set to commence in August 2027. Prospective candidates are free to propose their own research projects, that should fall broadly within the larger research interests of the department. Department of Communication and Culture , where the candidate will be based, is currently home to about 50 faculty. The Department is highly international in its faculty composition as well as its ongoing research and industry collaborations. The department hosts research groups within Internet and Society, Corporate Communication, Creative Industries, as well as Education Management. Ongoing research in the department is for instance concerned with the role of the arts in the digital transformation, the structural changes of the creative industries, the roles of communication technologies in shaping the future of work and new forms of labour and organizations, online organizing and communities, social legitimacy of technological transformations, and innovation in education management. The members of the department regularly publish on such issues in the field’s top journals, including among others the Journal of Management, Journal of Management Information Systems, Human Relations, Organization Studies, California Management Review, Work, Employment and Society, Human Resource Management, Human Resource Management Journal, Journal of Applied Psychology, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Leadership Quarterly, Journal of Management Studies, and Business Ethics Quarterly. The four-year program is designed for talented students who wish to pursue an international career within academia and who can contribute to the international arena with their research and publications. The recruitment of our PhD students is an important element of the department’s research agenda, as part of our goal to meet BI’s vision of being one of the leading business schools in Europe. Eligible applicants must have completed a Master of Science degree with thesis work, a research masters/M. Phil degree, or a comparable degree relevant for the specialization in Communication (comprising such disciplines such as management, communication studies, political sciences, psychology, sociology, and philosophy) by the early summer of 2027. An MBA degree does not fulfil the requirements for admission. Final year Master of Science students are encouraged to apply. Accepted applicants will be offered close supervision and follow-up by the research faculty. The four-year scholarships are currently NOK 623,200- per year (will be adjusted during 2027). The positions provide for automatic membership in the Norwegian Public Service Pension Fund ( Statens Pensjonskasse ). The scholarships require 25% of the teaching responsibilities of a full-time professor position. PhD candidates will have their place of work at BI Norwegian Business School in Oslo, Norway. Additional information about the doctoral programme, admission requirements and the application can be obtained at info@bi.no and the department’s website. Candidates are asked to upload the following information with their application: Certificate of a Master of Science degree or equivalent, including transcripts of grades. Certificate of a Bachelor’s degree or equivalent, including transcript of grades. A Diploma Supplement or a similar document describing in detail the study and grade system and the rights for further studies associated with the obtained degree. A project proposal (5-10 pages including topic, proposed method, schedule). CV. Letters of recommendations from relevant employers/tutors providing evidence of your skills as a researcher (a minimum of 2 letters). Please arrange with the people submitting recommendation letters to email their recommendations to phd.communication@bi.no by the application deadline. Certificates from previously completed courses at the doctoral level, if requesting approval of these for the PhD program at BI Norwegian Business School (see section 2 in our PhD Regulations). If you have taken any courses at PhD level please complete the following form (maximum 18 ECTS). A complete list of all publications and/or other documented relevant activities. Signed verification document. Test scores TOEFL/IELTS (conditions for a TOEFL / IELTS waiver here: Language requirements ) Please note that all documents must be uploaded in the electronic application. Documents may not be submitted by e-mail. Furthermore, note that any documents forwarded after the application deadline will not be considered. Exceptions will only be made for students who are completing their master’s degree in 2027 and do not have a final certificate when applying. Please note that you will not be able to revise your application once it has been submitted. Candidates may, at a later stage, be asked to forward further information and/or be called in for an interview. Candidates who are accepted for the program, must provide a more detailed progress plan with milestones and courses for the four years of study. BI Norwegian Business School is ranked as Norway’s #1 business school and one of the best in Europe. With more than 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000 alumni, it is also one of the largest and most influential business schools in Europe. BI is considered the main provider of business education in Norway, offering a diverse and comprehensive portfolio of bachelor’s, master’s, PhD and executive study programmes and courses. Our different partnerships and collaborations with leading Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions further enhance the quality of our study programmes. Towards 2030, BI aims to deliver knowledge that truly makes a difference through world-class research and outstanding learning experiences, giving businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the opportunity to build meaningful careers. Print Send application Share on: Region: Oslo Job type: Fixed Term Contract Working hours: Full-time Working days: Day Application deadline: 01/12/2026 Expected start date: 16/08/2027 Location: Campus Oslo Contacts: Christian Fieseler Mobile: +47 46410088 Company homepage: https://www.bi.no/ Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet - Doktorgrad BI Norwegian Business School is ranked as Norway’s #1 business school and one of the best in Europe. With more than 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000 alumni, it is also one of the largest and most influential business schools in Europe. BI is considered the main provider of business education in Norway, offering a diverse and comprehensive portfolio of bachelor’s, master’s, PhD and executive study programmes and courses. Our different partnerships and collaborations with leading Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions further enhance the quality of our study programmes. Towards 2030, BI aims to deliver knowledge that truly makes a difference through world-class research and outstanding learning experiences, giving businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the opportunity to build meaningful careers. Back to the top English Latvian Danish Czech Dutch Estonian German Spanish Swedish Finnish French Italian Lithuanian Norwegian Polish × This website uses cookies We use cookies to personalise content, ads and to analyse our traffic. We also share information about your use of our site with our advertising and analytics partners who may combine it with other information that you’ve provided to them or that they’ve collected from your use of their services. Privacy Policy Show details Hide details Save and close Accept all Decline all"
    },
    "https://bi.easycruit.com/vacancy/3660173/200453?iso=no": {
      "title": "Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet",
      "description": "Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet - Doktorgrad  - PhD Candidate in Data and Decision Sciences PhD Candidate in Data and Decision Sciences Send application BI invites applications for doctoral scholarships in Data and Decision Sciences, affiliated with the Department of Data Science and Analytics. BI Norwegian Business School is one of Europe's largest educational institutions, with over 20.000 students. As Norway's leading business school, BI builds on a unique tradition of combining academic rigour and professional relevance. Our programmes range from bachelor's to master's and PhD programmes. BI is also known for its many customized executive education programmes. BI boasts some of Europe's leading academic departments within the fields of data science, operations research, economics, finance, strategy, marketing, and management. As an employee at BI Norwegian Business School, you will meet exciting challenges in an engaging and international environment, with over 1000 colleagues who continuously push the frontiers of knowledge. PhD Candidates in Data and Decision Sciences BI Norwegian Business School invites applications for limited number of doctoral scholarships affiliated with the Department of Data Science and Analytics. The appointment is a full-time position for a period of four years. The place of work is BI's Oslo campus and starting date is August 2027. Department of Data Science and Analytics The department is committed to research at the highest international level. The faculty members' interests cover a wide range of fields in modern data science and business analytics, with a strong quantitative emphasis. The department enjoys close connections with industry and public sector, with unique collaborations within retail, transportation and energy. The department runs an international weekly research seminar series in which academics from the world's best research institutions present their work. These seminars and other visits by international researchers give PhD candidates an excellent opportunity to reflect and receive feedback on their own research. The department also regularly organizes conferences and workshops. The department hosts AMOR, the Interdisciplinary Center for Applied Mathematics and Operations Research. Faculty at the Department of Accounting and Operations Management at BI is actively involved in the PhD specialization and activities in the AMOR centre with several collaborative projects with the department and industry. This facilitates a broad and active research environment for the PhD candidates. Embedded in the AMOR center is SURE-AI - Center for Sustainable, Risk-Averse and Ethical AI, a Norwegian AI centre funded by the Research Council of Norway (2025-2030). SURE-AI comprises around 50 faculty members from well-renowned higher education institutions in Norway, in close collaboration with industry and the public sector. The centre sponsors and supports faculty research groups, conferences, and seminars at the department, and provide excellent collaboration opportunities for the PhD candidates. PhD specialization in Data and Decision Sciences The PhD specialization in Data and Decision Sciences prepares candidates for careers in the world's leading academic institutions, research-oriented international and national organizations, and the industry. The specialization is a unique blend of modern data science and research in business decisions and analytics. The four-year program offers rigorous training for candidates with strong analytical skills and intellectual curiosity. It follows a standard structure in place at all comparable programs around the world. The first year is devoted to course work that covers all the major fields in data science and operations research and core topics in machine learning and computer science relevant for a PhD in Data and Decision Sciences. These courses are mainly taught by BI faculty. The candidates can also take specialized courses and participate in doctoral workshops through for example the Norwegian Artificial Intelligence Research Consortium (NORA). The second year of the program sees candidates transitioning to research work. The candidates will work towards the doctoral dissertation that is typically a collection of three research articles. Research work is done in close co-operation with the supervisor and other faculty members from the department. Projects joint with faculty members may involve collaborators from other research institutions. Candidates also participate in weekly research seminars with international scholars and present their research work at departmental workshops. The research environment is supportive, and PhD candidates take active part in all the social life at the department. Additional information, including detailed course plans, may be found here . Funding: The four-year scholarship is set according to the Norwegian State Salary Scale and currently pays NOK 623.200 annually (will be adjusted in 2027). The position is linked to The Norwegian Public Service Pension Fund (Statens Pensjonskasse). The scholarship involves 25% teaching obligation. Application timeline and submission rules: The application and its attached documents can be submitted only electronically by using \"Send Application\" button on the right-hand side in this announcement. E-mail or copy applications will not be accepted. Kindly note that all documents need to have reached the Doctoral Administration deadline stated in this announcement in order to be considered. The only exception to this rule is candidates who are completing their master's degree in 2027 and do not have a final certificate when applying. You will not be able to revise your application once it has been submitted. Application requirements: We encourage applications from candidates who have solid quantitative skills and a strong background in fields/disciplines such as statistics, operations research, machine learning, computer science, finance, economics and mathematics. The successful candidates should have a genuine interest in doing fundamental research within applied business areas. Strong programming, communication and analytical skills are also crucial for successful completion of the program. If applicants are otherwise equally qualified, female applicants will be given preference. The following list details the formal application requirements: A. Academic record Eligible applicants must have completed a Master of Science degree with thesis work, a Research Masters/M.Phil degree, or a comparable degree relevant for the PhD specialization in Data and Decision Sciences by the time the program starts in early autumn of 2027, with a grade point average of B or higher. An MBA degree does not fulfill the requirements for admission. B. GRE/GMAT Applicants who hold a master's degree from an institution in an EU/EEA country are strongly encouraged to take either the GMAT or the GRE test. Applicants whose master's degree is not from an institution in an EU/EEA country are required to take either the GMAT or the GRE test. We will need percentile scores and raw scores for the Verbal, Quantitative and Analytical Writing sections of the GRE or GMAT to consider your application. Incomplete sections or partial scores are not sufficient to consider your application. A \"good score\" is generally considered to be 85% and higher. However, there is no minimum cutoff score for the GRE/GMAT in order for your file to be reviewed. C. TOEFL/IELTS Applicants must take either TOEFL or IELTS. The minimum standards for test scores acceptable for admission are: TOEFL a total score of 575 points for the written test or 233 for the computer-based version or 90 points on the internet-based test IELTS a score of 6.5 Exemptions are made for applicants: whose native language is English who have two years or more of higher education where the language of instruction was English from a country which is a member of the EU/EEA and/or the Council of Europe/UNESCO-Cepes, who have English as the first foreign language taken over a period of at least 7 years in primary school, secondary school and upper secondary education. Under certain circumstances, applicants may request a waiver for the TOEFL or IELTS when applying for admission. To request a TOEFL/IELTS waiver, the applicant must submit a waiver form. TOEFL/IETLS scores must be from within the last two years. The codes for BI Norwegian Business School are as follows: GMAT 0529, TOEFL 0529, GRE 7365. For IELTS we accept this if the TRF number is visible. D. Materials to be uploaded in the electronic application You are required to upload the following electronically with your application: CV, recommendation letters, statement of purpose, and selected academic work Full CV/resume. In addition to the usual items, this should include a complete list of all research work, including publications (if any), thesis work, and other documented relevant research activities. Letters of recommendations from people who can assess your suitability for doctoral studies. These people would ideally by academics who have taught you, supervised your research work, or have other relevant information about your potential as a researcher. If such people are not available, non-academic professional people can also provide a letter with an emphasis on your research potential. A minimum of two letters is required. Please arrange with the people submitting recommendation letters to email their recommendations to phd.datascience@bi.no by the application deadline. Statement of purpose describing your plans and motivation for PhD studies and your career objectives. The statement should be written in English and should not exceed 1000 words. One selected academic work showcasing your previous academic output. This can be a copy of your master's thesis or other relevant research work. Certificates, test results, and verification document Certificate of a Master of Science degree or equivalent, including transcript of grades. Certificate of a bachelor's degree or equivalent, including transcript of grades. A Diploma supplement or a similar document, describing in detail the study and grade system and the rights for further studies associated with the obtained degree. Other relevant certificates and transcripts Certificates from previously completed courses at the doctoral level, if requesting approval of these for the PhD programme at BI Norwegian Business School (see section 2 in our PhD Regulations). If you have taken any courses at PhD level, please complete the following form (maximum 18 ECTS). Test scores GMAT/GRE and TOEFL/IELTS (if these are not sent directly by the test center) signed verification document Interviews and additional information Candidates may, at a later stage, be asked to forward further information and/or be called in for an interview. Information about the doctoral program and admission requirements can be obtained from the Doctoral Administration at BI Norwegian Business School. E-mail: info@bi.no HANDELSH ØYSKOLEN BI PROGRAMOMR ÅDET DOKTORGRAD BI Norwegian Business School is ranked as Norway's #1 business school and one of the best in Europe. With more than 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000 alumni, it is also one of the largest and most influential business schools in Europe. BI is considered the main provider of business education in Norway, offering a diverse and comprehensive portfolio of bachelor's, master's, PhD and executive study programmes and courses. Our different partnerships and collaborations with leading Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions further enhance the quality of our study programmes. Towards 2030, BI aims to deliver knowledge that truly makes a difference through world-class research and outstanding learning experiences, giving businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the opportunity to build meaningful careers. Print Send application Share on: Region: Oslo Job type: Fixed Term Contract Working hours: Full-time Working days: Day Application deadline: 01/12/2026 Expected start date: 16/08/2027 Location: Campus Oslo Contacts: Fred Espen Benth Mobile: +47 99262384 Company homepage: https://www.bi.no/ Handelshøyskolen BI Programområdet - Doktorgrad BI Norwegian Business School is ranked as Norway’s #1 business school and one of the best in Europe. With more than 20.000 students, 1000 employees and 300.000 alumni, it is also one of the largest and most influential business schools in Europe. BI is considered the main provider of business education in Norway, offering a diverse and comprehensive portfolio of bachelor’s, master’s, PhD and executive study programmes and courses. Our different partnerships and collaborations with leading Norwegian and international companies, organisations and institutions further enhance the quality of our study programmes. Towards 2030, BI aims to deliver knowledge that truly makes a difference through world-class research and outstanding learning experiences, giving businesses the knowledge to succeed and people the opportunity to build meaningful careers. Back to the top English Latvian Danish Czech Dutch Estonian German Spanish Swedish Finnish French Italian Lithuanian Norwegian Polish × This website uses cookies We use cookies to personalise content, ads and to analyse our traffic. We also share information about your use of our site with our advertising and analytics partners who may combine it with other information that you’ve provided to them or that they’ve collected from your use of their services. Privacy Policy Show details Hide details Save and close Accept all Decline all"
